('For type hints only, `if typing.TYPE_CHECKING:` imports avoid runtime cycles, but treat that as a sign to look at the design, not a fix.', 'For type-only dependencies, TYPE_CHECKING can avoid executing imports. Annotation evaluation must also be handled: older Python versions may need quoted/postponed annotations, and runtime get_type_hints still needs the referenced names. Python 3.14 defers annotations by default. This can be an appropriate type-only solution; it does not remove genuine runtime coupling.'),
